Two refinements to the MemorySlot/Direct indirect-call distinction:

- A Direct target with a non-zero offset into the callee (computed-
  goto-style block addresses never interpose) now preserves the offset
  and skips @PLT: the PLT entry is only defined for offset 0, and the
  previous code silently DROPPED the offset whenever the symbol needed
  the PLT — calling sym instead of sym+off.

- tests/regression/indirect_call_global_target.c pins both shapes
  end-to-end: the inlined-store DirectGlobal shape (the 10-suite
  SIGSEGV class), a real GlobalCell table, and a GEP-offset cell.
